  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 is the strongest evidence so far (≈0.653 acc/0.628 F1), while the only multimodal test with ResNet50, avgpool, and concat is slightly below it (0.6315 acc/0.6068 F1), leaving uncertainty about whether the image modality can help or whether concat fusion is the bottleneck. config_031 changes only fusion to weighted, holding RNA encoder, profile setting, image encoder, and aggregation fixed, so it directly tests whether adaptive fusion can make the multimodal model competitive. This one-factor extension of the existing multimodal result is the most efficient next use of budget before moving to new image encoders or aggregation choices."
}

